  "review": [
    "Fletcher entered service in 1942; the five named Form 10s cannot all be treated as a simultaneous December 1941 force.",
    "The Mahan Annex lists class-wide search radar during 1942 and deletion of the beam gun in late 1942; Drayton and Perkins cards show the deletion on earlier named refits. Determine the exact desired narrative date before resolving Lamson radar fit and main battery.",
    "The Annex records Lamson as the only Mahan hull that actually had the late-1945 two-rack deletion; this is not its December 1941 setup.",
    "Gridley 1942 SC and late 1943 Mk4 entries identify Craven, not Maury. Do not copy them to Maury.",
    "Tassafaronga source PDF 75 confirms all five named ships fought in the same US force, and identifies the Gridley, Mahan and Fletcher classes. Its 1942-11-30 date is a candidate, not a declared prologue date."
  ],
